msgid "Warn about a broken spam check"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/settings-page.php:373
msgid "Send a warning once this many submissions in a row have been rejected as spam. Real spam arrives in bursts; a check that has stopped working rejects everything, so an unbroken run is evidence about the check rather than about the senders. Set to 0 to never warn."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/settings-page.php:374
msgid "Let Site Health test the reCAPTCHA key against Google"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/settings-page.php:375
msgid "Off by default because it sends your Contact Form 7 reCAPTCHA secret key to Google in order to ask whether the key is still accepted. That is the only request this plugin ever makes to Google. With it off, Site Health still reports a run of spam rejections, which is the same symptom without the third party."
